course: dictionary
lesson: 9846
title: Swoop: fast and sudden
level: primary-5
stars: 0
explain: A word can have different jobs in a sentence. Swoop can be a verb, which is an action, or a noun, which is a thing or an event. Read the words around it to find out which job it does.
explain: «The gull swoops down and snatches a chip.» Swoops is a verb here, because the gull is doing an action. Down shows the direction, and snatches shows it happens quickly. So swoop means to fly or move down quickly and suddenly, usually to catch something.
explain: Swoop can also be a noun: «The hawk made a swoop at the mouse.» A swoop is a quick downward rush or a sudden attack. When you see a or the before the word, it is probably a noun.
explain: Try the swap check. Put «flies down quickly» in place of swoops: «An eagle flies down quickly with a fierce scream.» It still makes sense, so you have found the right meaning.
fact: To swoop means to fly or move down quickly and suddenly, usually to catch something.
fact: Swoop can be a verb (swoops, swooped, swooping) or a noun (a swoop).
fact: Useful phrases are swoop down, swoop in, swoop on, and in one fell swoop.
fact: «In one fell swoop» means all at once.
fact: In spring, some birds such as magpies may swoop at people near their nests to protect their chicks. Stay calm, cover your head, and walk away.
exercise: «In a nature film, an eagle swoops down with a fierce scream.» What does swoops mean? | Sings a long, soft song | Sleeps all day in a tall tree | *Flies down quickly and suddenly to catch something
exercise: «The hawk made a swoop at the mouse.» What kind of word is swoop in this sentence? | An adjective, a describing word | *A noun, a thing or event | A verb, an action word
exercise: «The gull swoops down and snatches a chip.» Find and copy one word that means grab quickly. | chip | *snatches | seaside | gull
test: «He wanted to finish the whole job in one fell swoop.» What does the phrase mean? | Very slowly, one step at a time | On a windy day | *All at once
test: Why might a magpie swoop at people in spring? | To look for worms in the grass | *To protect its nest and chicks | To say hello to them
exam: Which sentence uses swoop as a noun? | The bird began to swoop | They swoop down to the river | The owl will swoop at dawn | *The owl's swoop caught a mouse before it could run
